  "query_preview": "..FOR EXTREME SOUTHWESTERN CALIFORNIA INCLUDING ORANGE...\nSAN DIEGO...WESTERN RIVERSIDE AND SOUTHWESTERN SAN BERNARDINO\nCOUNTIES...\n\n...UPDATED AVIATION DISCUSSION...\n\nA slow cooling trend begins on Thursday as the upper ridge begins\nto weaken. However, this humid, tropical airmass will remain in \nplace through Friday. Therefore, areas of major HeatRisk will \ncontinue through Thursday for the coastal basin and through Friday\nfor the low deserts. By Saturday, an upper trough to the \nnorthwest will begin to push the weakening ridge out of the region\nbringing more relief from the heat and humidity. High \ntemperatures will fall 5 to 10 degrees below normal across the \nregion from Sunday into early next week.\n\nMorning marine layer clouds and fog will likely begin to reform \nover coastal waters as moderate onshore flow returns from Friday \nonward. There is a chance for fog Saturday morning for coastal \nareas and western valleys. Thereafter, the marine layer should \ndeepen further into early next week with low clouds filling most \nof the coastal basin each morning. Additionally, breezy conditions\nare expected for outer coastal waters, mountains, and deserts \nover the weekend. By late next week model solutions diverge, but \nthe mean of the guidance tilts toward high pressure and monsoonal \nmoisture building back into the region from the east.",
